\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Define a monoidal Segal-category presentation and its unbiased tensor multimaps through the chosen categorical interface. Construct Mat(V) with its explicit size, coherence, and map comparisons; identify its monads with enriched categories.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Cartesian examples should validate the shared infrastructure first.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Treating a weak tensor presentation as a strict functor without comparison.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{A precisely stated Gepner–Haugseng comparison, assigned an acceptance ID when this later track is activated.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{later (\ref{ms-0007}+).}
}
